WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.235 --> 00:00:16.476
Jack opened his eyes.

2
00:00:17.256 --> 00:00:19.678
He was in his living room, and it was daytime.

3
00:00:19.838 --> 00:00:21.699
He must have fallen asleep on the couch.

4
00:00:22.719 --> 00:00:24.560
He glanced at the clock on the TV.

5
00:00:25.181 --> 00:00:25.741
Oh no!

6
00:00:25.761 --> 00:00:28.682
"Mom! I'll be late for swim practice!"

7
00:00:29.083 --> 00:00:29.683
he called out.

8
00:00:29.703 --> 00:00:31.304
"I know."

9
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.682
His mother walked into the room from the kitchen.

10
00:00:36.284 --> 00:00:39.406
"You must be exhausted from your early-morning heroism.

11
00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:41.268
I didn't want to wake you up."

12
00:00:42.289 --> 00:00:43.189
"Have you heard how Mrs.

13
00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:43.990
Wilson is doing?"

14
00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:44.871
Jack asked.

15
00:00:44.891 --> 00:00:47.613
"She's getting checked out in the hospital.

16
00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:54.599
I heard she's giving everyone a very hard time, ordering around the doctors and nurses and demanding a

17
00:00:54.639 --> 00:00:56.620
larger TV and softer sheets."

18
00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.784
"I can definitely picture that," Jack said.

19
00:01:01.736 --> 00:01:04.717
"She should be out of the hospital soon," his mother said.

20
00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:06.098
She smiled.

21
00:01:06.118 --> 00:01:09.479
"The poor doctors and nurses probably can't wait to get rid of her!"

22
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.060
"Yeah," Jack said.

23
00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:16.242
"I wonder what happened though, how she ended up unconscious."

24
00:01:16.262 --> 00:01:20.744
"Maybe she bumped her head or had a problem with her heart," Mrs.

25
00:01:20.784 --> 00:01:21.444
Gibson said.

26
00:01:22.124 --> 00:01:24.065
"I have a feeling that she'll be fine."

27
00:01:25.006 --> 00:01:26.886
His mother looked closely at Jack.

28
00:01:26.906 --> 00:01:30.408
"You should skip practice today and get some rest."

29
00:01:31.348 --> 00:01:32.229
Jack shook his head.

30
00:01:32.249 --> 00:01:33.970
"I need to get to the pool.

31
00:01:34.311 --> 00:01:36.653
I've missed too many swim team practices already."

32
00:01:37.613 --> 00:01:43.538
Even though he couldn't compete in Saturday's meet against the Pacific Piranhas, he wanted to support his team

33
00:01:43.819 --> 00:01:46.161
and show Coach Shin he was responsible.

34
00:01:47.822 --> 00:01:48.603
His mother nodded.

35
00:01:48.623 --> 00:01:52.486
"Okay. But promise me you'll take it easy."

36
00:01:53.307 --> 00:01:58.391
By the time Jack arrived at the community pool, he was a half hour late and his teammates

37
00:01:58.431 --> 00:01:59.352
were already swimming.

38
00:01:59.964 --> 00:02:01.725
"It's about time you showed up, Jack!"

39
00:02:02.286 --> 00:02:03.047
Hulk bellowed.

40
00:02:03.807 --> 00:02:10.032
He hurled his giant body out of the water and hurried toward Jack, leaving large puddles along the

41
00:02:10.072 --> 00:02:13.775
way. "Yikes!"

42
00:02:14.296 --> 00:02:15.516
Jack thought, backing up.

43
00:02:15.537 --> 00:02:17.858
"What is Hulk so mad about?

44
00:02:18.259 --> 00:02:20.480
Is he going to yell at me for being late to practice?"

45
00:02:21.461 --> 00:02:26.986
The huge swimmer stood in front of Jack, his meaty face tense as he stared down.

46
00:02:27.006 --> 00:02:30.296
"You're Jack Gibson, right?"

47
00:02:30.657 --> 00:02:31.277
Hulk asked.

48
00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:34.860
"That's me," Jack squeaked like a baby mouse.

49
00:02:36.882 --> 00:02:38.543
Hulk lunged toward him.

50
00:02:39.504 --> 00:02:43.907
The movement was so sudden that this time Jack didn't have time to back away.

51
00:02:45.148 --> 00:02:45.769
"Here goes!"

52
00:02:46.209 --> 00:02:47.750
Jack thought as he shut his eyes.

53
00:02:48.491 --> 00:02:53.815
Getting tackled onto the hard pool deck by a gigantic brute was bound to hurt—a lot.

54
00:02:55.136 --> 00:02:57.278
He didn't want to watch his own bones breaking.

55
00:02:58.699 --> 00:03:00.380
But Hulk didn't tackle him.

56
00:03:01.041 --> 00:03:05.923
Instead he wrapped his giant arms around Jack's slim body and hugged him hard.

57
00:03:07.803 --> 00:03:09.604
Water dripped all over Jack.

58
00:03:12.185 --> 00:03:14.386
"Why in the world is he hugging me?"

59
00:03:14.686 --> 00:03:15.306
Jack thought.

60
00:03:16.247 --> 00:03:17.247
"Um what's up?"

61
00:03:17.787 --> 00:03:18.548
Jack squeaked.

62
00:03:19.168 --> 00:03:20.208
"My grammy.

63
00:03:20.649 --> 00:03:23.830
My wonderful grandmother is alive today because of you.

64
00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.531
You saved her life."

65
00:03:27.491 --> 00:03:28.912
"Huh?" Jack said.

66
00:03:29.568 --> 00:03:30.709
His eyes blinked open.

67
00:03:30.729 --> 00:03:36.493
"My grandmother told me you rescued her from the bottom of the swimming pool in her new apartment

68
00:03:36.513 --> 00:03:40.416
building. I can't thank you enough," Hulk said.

69
00:03:40.436 --> 00:03:42.617
"She means so much to me.

70
00:03:42.878 --> 00:03:47.521
She taught me how to swim and coaches me and—" "Wait."

71
00:03:47.901 --> 00:03:50.243
Jack, shocked, took a step backward.

72
00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:53.625
"Mrs. Wilson is your grandmother?"

73
00:03:54.566 --> 00:03:56.267
"Yes. Can't you tell?

74
00:03:56.387 --> 00:03:57.528
I'm built just like her."

75
00:03:58.564 --> 00:04:04.646
Now that Jack thought about it, they were built alike—like a pair of King Kong monsters.

76
00:04:06.566 --> 00:04:15.929
Mrs. Wilson's bragging came rushing back to him: "My grandson, little Tommy, once swam 196 days in a

77
00:04:16.049 --> 00:04:20.350
row You should see my grandson do the butterfly.

78
00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:26.512
Little Tommy is like beauty in motion Jack stared at Hulk.

79
00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:29.081
"Are you You can't be.

80
00:04:29.681 --> 00:04:32.063
You're not little Tommy, are you?"

81
00:04:32.563 --> 00:04:33.043
he asked.

82
00:04:33.063 --> 00:04:34.665
"I am.

83
00:04:35.265 --> 00:04:37.847
My real name is Thomas, but everyone calls me Hulk.

84
00:04:39.108 --> 00:04:40.308
Except my sweet grammy.

85
00:04:41.109 --> 00:04:44.351
She's always called me little Tommy or sugar or sweetie."

86
00:04:45.392 --> 00:04:47.033
Hulk wiped a tear from his cheek.

87
00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:49.695
"I don't know what I'd do without my grammy.

88
00:04:51.116 --> 00:04:58.508
She makes the best cherry pie and shows me videos of herself swimming in the Olympics and—" "Mrs.

89
00:04:58.568 --> 00:05:00.150
Wilson swam in the Olympics?"

90
00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:02.651
Jack asked, even more shocked.

91
00:05:02.671 --> 00:05:04.893
"Two different Olympics."

92
00:05:05.253 --> 00:05:08.716
Hulk, also known as little Tommy, smiled proudly.

93
00:05:08.736 --> 00:05:15.300
"One year she came in fourth in the breaststroke, missing a medal by one one-hundredth of a second."

94
00:05:15.961 --> 00:05:17.802
"Wow!" Jack exclaimed.

95
00:05:17.822 --> 00:05:19.503
"That's amazing!"

96
00:05:20.064 --> 00:05:21.244
Coach Shin walked over.

97
00:05:21.264 --> 00:05:26.068
"Hulk, get back in the pool," he said sternly.

98
00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:28.201
Then he pointed at Jack.

99
00:05:28.221 --> 00:05:31.844
"You skipped the first thirty minutes of practice today.

100
00:05:32.905 --> 00:05:34.706
You're already missing Saturday's meet.

101
00:05:35.147 --> 00:05:37.829
If you can't get here on time, you'll miss the next meet too."

102
00:05:37.849 --> 00:05:42.333
"Coach Shin and everyone else, I have an announcement," Hulk said loudly.

103
00:05:42.353 --> 00:05:47.737
"Early this morning Jack found my grandmother unconscious on the bottom of a swimming pool.

104
00:05:48.277 --> 00:05:50.039
He dived in and pulled her out.

105
00:05:50.619 --> 00:05:51.600
He saved her life."

106
00:05:53.301 --> 00:05:54.943
"Awesome!" a girl said.

107
00:05:54.963 --> 00:05:57.129
"Wow!" a boy said.

108
00:05:57.149 --> 00:06:00.612
"Hulk, wasn't your grandmother an Olympic swimmer?"

109
00:06:01.012 --> 00:06:01.833
the coach asked.

110
00:06:02.774 --> 00:06:03.434
Hulk nodded.

111
00:06:04.135 --> 00:06:07.197
"More importantly, she's the best grammy ever."

112
00:06:08.058 --> 00:06:09.319
He wiped away another tear.

113
00:06:09.339 --> 00:06:11.301
"Jack saved her life.

114
00:06:12.102 --> 00:06:13.042
He's a real hero.

115
00:06:13.783 --> 00:06:16.986
Coach, you should let him compete in Saturday's meet."

116
00:06:17.947 --> 00:06:20.269
"He deserves it," Laura chimed in quickly.

117
00:06:20.289 --> 00:06:22.370
"Jack lives in my apartment building.

118
00:06:22.791 --> 00:06:23.932
So does Hulk's grandmother.

119
00:06:24.712 --> 00:06:27.153
She's a very large woman, almost as big as Hulk.

120
00:06:28.254 --> 00:06:32.835
Jack pulled her from the bottom of the pool, swam with her to the edge, and got her

121
00:06:32.935 --> 00:06:33.596
out of the water.

122
00:06:34.236 --> 00:06:36.197
That shows what a strong swimmer he is."

123
00:06:36.217 --> 00:06:39.858
"Coach, I've been practicing on my own.

124
00:06:40.258 --> 00:06:42.019
Watch this," Jack said eagerly.

125
00:06:42.759 --> 00:06:44.660
He hurried to the pool and dived in.

126
00:06:46.821 --> 00:06:52.843
He swam the breaststroke with his hands cupped more carefully and his head further down, just like Mrs.

127
00:06:52.903 --> 00:06:55.617
Wilson, the Olympian, had told him to do.

128
00:06:56.597 --> 00:06:58.038
He zipped across the pool.

129
00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:05.822
As Jack got out of the water, Hulk and Laura and some of the other swimmers clapped and

130
00:07:05.882 --> 00:07:06.543
cheered for him.

131
00:07:10.945 --> 00:07:11.765
The coach nodded.

132
00:07:11.785 --> 00:07:13.927
"Much improved," he said.

133
00:07:13.947 --> 00:07:17.729
"Our relay team needs him on breaststroke," Hulk said.

134
00:07:17.749 --> 00:07:23.592
"And having a hero at the meet would be good publicity for the team," Laura added.

135
00:07:25.024 --> 00:07:25.804
The coach frowned.

136
00:07:26.604 --> 00:07:30.966
"I'm not sure the Sharks need any publicity, Laura, but I agree with you.

137
00:07:32.046 --> 00:07:36.107
Jack has shown some serious swimming skills and hard work."

138
00:07:36.847 --> 00:07:37.807
He nodded at Jack.

139
00:07:37.827 --> 00:07:39.028
"All right.

140
00:07:39.068 --> 00:07:40.868
Jack, you can swim in the meet."

141
00:07:41.849 --> 00:07:43.169
"Yes!" Jack cried.

142
00:07:43.189 --> 00:07:44.689
"Thank you, Coach Shin!"

143
00:07:45.269 --> 00:07:46.450
The team clapped again.

144
00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:53.011
"Let's celebrate by singing Jack's favorite song," one of the guys said.

145
00:07:53.652 --> 00:08:02.310
He started singing, "'Baby, don't you see, you're my destiny.'"

146
00:08:03.551 --> 00:08:04.872
More kids sang along.

147
00:08:04.892 --> 00:08:07.975
"'Listen to my pleas.

148
00:08:08.755 --> 00:08:13.059
You're the one for me.'"

149
00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:19.164
Jack joined in on, "'Ooh, baby, baby, baby.'"

150
00:08:20.105 --> 00:08:23.728
Soon everyone was laughing too hard to keep singing.
